/// A collection method called with too few arguments raises, catchably.
///
/// Issue #27.  Same rule and same sentence as ArityFunction.a24 and
/// ArityBuiltin.a24 -- ALGOL-24.md lists 'Expected 1 arguments but got 0.'
/// under Run-time errors, so it is raised as a String and a handler for String
/// catches it.  A collection method is a call like any other and nothing in the
/// specification gives it a different rule.
///
/// ⚠️ Compiled, this does not fail.  It CRASHES -- SIGSEGV, exit 139, no
/// output at all.  'collection_method' (bootstrap/algol.c:2345) opens with
/// '(void)count;' and every branch below then indexes args[0]; a
/// zero-argument call arrives with args == NULL.  This is the only defect in
/// the repository that crashes rather than producing a wrong answer or a
/// refusal, and it is reachable from a three-line program.
///
/// ⚠️ Kept in its own file BECAUSE it crashes.  A segfault takes the process
/// down, so any test block after it in the same file never reports -- the
/// harness would show one silent failure where there are several.  Same reason
/// ArityBuiltin.a24 is separate from ArityFunction.a24, a different mechanism.
///
/// ⚠️ Get, Add and IndexOf are asserted together deliberately, and they are the
/// three that reach args[0] with no argument to read.  Any fix that guards one
/// by hand rather than checking 'count' for the whole table will pass the first
/// assertion and crash on the second, which is the point of listing three.
///
/// Interpreted: passes.
/// Compiled:    crashes before the first assertion is reached.
///
test 'A Collection Method With Too Few Arguments Raises';
begin
    var L := [1, 2, 3];
    var Caught := '';

    try
        L.Get ();
    except
        on E : String do Caught := E;
    end

    AssertEqual ('Expected 1 arguments but got 0.', Caught);

    Caught := '';
    try
        L.Add ();
    except
        on E : String do Caught := E;
    end

    AssertEqual ('Expected 1 arguments but got 0.', Caught);

    Caught := '';
    try
        L.IndexOf ();
    except
        on E : String do Caught := E;
    end

    AssertEqual ('Expected 1 arguments but got 0.', Caught);
end
